range demonstrate that objective weight selection meaningfully shifts the campaign architecture.

Reducing total launches by consolidating payload onto fewer heavy-lift vehicles tends to lengthen
the campaign because cargo arrives less frequently. Schedule-minimal solutions saturate the
pad-turnaround constraint and push launch count toward its upper bound.
Cost-optimal solutions substitute cheaper vehicles (New Glenn $90 M, Crew Dragon $220 M/mission)
wherever capacity allows, avoiding SLS Block 2 ($4,100 M) except when launch count dominates.

